WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.221 --> 00:00:01.706
- How would I describe this?

00:00:01.706 --> 00:00:02.645
- Great.

00:00:02.645 --> 00:00:05.454
(rock music)

00:00:05.454 --> 00:00:07.257
- For those of you who don't know,

00:00:07.257 --> 00:00:09.039
Taiwan does not play
when it comes to food.

00:00:09.039 --> 00:00:11.152
So, I thought it would be fun
to invite some of my friends

00:00:11.152 --> 00:00:12.080
who've never had it before

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.294
and see what they think of it.

00:00:13.294 --> 00:00:15.366
- I don't think I've
ever had Taiwanese food.

00:00:15.366 --> 00:00:16.661
- I've had Chinese food.

00:00:16.661 --> 00:00:20.937
- I've probably had it
once without knowing it.

00:00:20.937 --> 00:00:22.779
- [Man In Plaid] Heysong Sarsaparilla.

00:00:22.779 --> 00:00:23.612
- Oh.

00:00:23.612 --> 00:00:24.555
- What.

00:00:24.555 --> 00:00:25.798
- This is root beer.

00:00:25.798 --> 00:00:26.831
- I want to put ice cream in it.

00:00:26.831 --> 00:00:28.114
- It's like bubble gum.

00:00:28.114 --> 00:00:30.041
- Bubble gum, some apple juice.

00:00:30.041 --> 00:00:31.783
- Bubble gum?

00:00:31.783 --> 00:00:32.897
- Bubble gum soda?

00:00:32.897 --> 00:00:34.383
- Yeah, a little bit like a cream soda?

00:00:34.383 --> 00:00:35.515
- [Girl In Gray] Yeah.

00:00:35.515 --> 00:00:38.311
- A little, like it's very, very sweet.

00:00:38.311 --> 00:00:40.455
- [Both Girls] Oooooh.

00:00:40.455 --> 00:00:41.901
- This looks like Korean pancakes.

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:42.876
- It's very buttery.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.024
- There's oil in between
every layer of this.

00:00:45.024 --> 00:00:45.857
- Yeah.

00:00:45.857 --> 00:00:46.899
- I would dip it in sauce.

00:00:46.899 --> 00:00:48.507
- Yeah, there's like flaky layers.

00:00:48.507 --> 00:00:50.054
- I feel uncomfortable
watching you peel it open.

00:00:50.054 --> 00:00:50.887
- Why?

00:00:50.887 --> 00:00:52.231
- I'm diggin' it.

00:00:52.231 --> 00:00:54.641
It reminds me a lot of latkas.

00:00:54.641 --> 00:00:56.390
- Every culture has
something like a tortilla.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:57.847
- This definitely tastes
asian as f&amp;@# though.

00:00:57.847 --> 00:00:59.612
(laughing)

00:00:59.612 --> 00:01:00.779
- [Girl In Gray] Is that garlic?

00:01:00.779 --> 00:01:02.056
- Is it just straight up cloves of garlic?

00:01:02.056 --> 00:01:03.640
- It doesn't have like the spice taste

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:05.010
that a lot of sausages have.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:05.843
- Huh?

00:01:05.843 --> 00:01:06.676
- [Girl In Gray] You don't like it?

00:01:06.676 --> 00:01:07.675
- No, no it's not that I don't like it,

00:01:07.675 --> 00:01:09.637
I just haven't tasted this before.

00:01:09.637 --> 00:01:10.913
- It's kind of sweet.

00:01:10.913 --> 00:01:12.145
- But it's like a good sweet.

00:01:12.145 --> 00:01:14.269
- I don't get it, because
sausage is ground up.

00:01:14.269 --> 00:01:16.481
But this doesn't look ground
up, it looks like it was ham.

00:01:16.481 --> 00:01:17.979
- I love the garlic with it.

00:01:17.979 --> 00:01:19.035
- I'm not mad at this.

00:01:19.035 --> 00:01:19.868
- The garlic is strong.

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:22.727
- I love garlic, but it's a
decision to eat straight garlic.

00:01:22.727 --> 00:01:24.560
- Yeah, I'll eat that.

00:01:26.302 --> 00:01:27.714
- Oh my god, noodles.

00:01:27.714 --> 00:01:28.927
- It smells so good.

00:01:28.927 --> 00:01:30.250
- Is this bok choy?

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:32.282
- Funny because when I
eat that kind of food,

00:01:32.282 --> 00:01:33.507
I never eat the cabbage.

00:01:33.507 --> 00:01:36.264
- Why don't you eat the
cabbage? YB, it's great!

00:01:36.264 --> 00:01:37.182
- I really like this.

00:01:37.182 --> 00:01:38.302
- Refreshing and nature-y.

00:01:38.302 --> 00:01:40.252
- This is definitely like a
lighter dish you would have.

00:01:40.252 --> 00:01:43.033
- It's not too salty,
and it's not too sweet.

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:45.146
- It's good, you know,

00:01:45.146 --> 00:01:46.533
it's beef noodle soup.

00:01:46.533 --> 00:01:49.250
- The thing with pho, is that
the beef gets overcooked.

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:53.592
- Yeah I gotta take you
to better places then.

00:01:53.592 --> 00:01:54.425
- Oh, egg.

00:01:54.425 --> 00:01:55.508
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:56.535 --> 00:01:57.615
- This is like Bulgogi.

00:01:57.615 --> 00:01:59.148
- Yeah, I was about to say,
this looks kinda like Bulgogi.

00:01:59.148 --> 00:02:00.988
- Taiwanese food is really
similar to Korean food.

00:02:00.988 --> 00:02:01.821
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.496
(laughing)

00:02:03.496 --> 00:02:05.725
- I love dishes that have
multiple animals in them.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:08.627
- It almost melts in your
mouth 'cause it's just so soft.

00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:12.308
- As a kid, I always ate rice
and I always hated eating rice

00:02:12.308 --> 00:02:14.572
'cause then I'd always have
to like mix it with the meat

00:02:14.572 --> 00:02:15.477
and stuff like this,

00:02:15.477 --> 00:02:19.560
but this is like drenched
in like it's own sauce.

00:02:20.635 --> 00:02:22.201
- Yas, all the way.

00:02:22.201 --> 00:02:24.562
- There weren't like a million
ingredients in each thing,

00:02:24.562 --> 00:02:26.907
there were like three to five
ingredients in every dish,

00:02:26.907 --> 00:02:28.300
but they work very well together.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:29.635
- Just like a few ingredients,

00:02:29.635 --> 00:02:31.656
all happily chillin'
together in your mouth.

00:02:31.656 --> 00:02:33.571
- A plus plus.

00:02:33.571 --> 00:02:34.941
Get you some Taiwanese food

00:02:34.941 --> 00:02:36.723
or get you someone who
knows how to make authentic

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:38.000
Taiwanese food.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.508
- You can't have bland pork, you crazy?

00:02:40.508 --> 00:02:42.534
- Is it just going to be an ad for pork?

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:43.759
- Yeah!

00:02:43.759 --> 00:02:44.592
- Eat pork!

00:02:44.592 --> 00:02:45.739
- Yeah, yeah, I think that's

00:02:45.739 --> 00:02:46.818
- [Cameraman] Brought to you by pork.

00:02:46.818 --> 00:02:48.155
- Brought to you by pork.

